<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
   Android 12+ (API 31+) backup and device transfer rules.

   Everything this app persists is excluded, deliberately:

   Privacy. The data is selfies, matched photos of people's faces, and a
   database describing who matched whom. The app's whole premise is that face
   matching happens on the device and the photos never leave it, which was not
   true while the default backup behaviour was uploading all of it.

   Correctness. Auto backup has a 25MB per app quota and a job's matched
   photos routinely exceed that, so the database would restore while the
   photos it points at were dropped. That leaves a history grid full of cards
   referencing files that do not exist, which is worse than no history.

   Nothing is lost that cannot be rebuilt: the models re download, and a job
   can be re run from the user's own ZIP.

   allowBackup is also false in the manifest, so these rules are defence in
   depth rather than the only guard. They exist so that turning backup on
   later is a deliberate choice with the sensitive paths already named.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" path="snapfind.db" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="saved_matches" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="job_work" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="facesdk_models" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="database" path="snapfind.db" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="saved_matches" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="job_work" />
        <exclude domain="file" path="facesdk_models" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
